# Docs conventions

- `docs/PLAN.md` is the master instruction file; architecture docs define cross-cutting rules; `docs/modules/NN-*.md`
  define per-module scope. Keep them consistent: a change in one must be mirrored where referenced.
- Module doc template (keep headings in this order): Scope & sidebar mapping → Doctype inventory → Document flows &
  mappers → Posting rules → Statuses → Settings & defaults → Reports & dashboard → UI notes → Deviations from
  ERPNext → Implementation checklist.
- Cite ERPNext sources as repo-relative paths (`erpnext/accounts/doctype/sales_invoice/sales_invoice.py`), never as
  line numbers (they drift).
- Tables for inventories; prose only for rationale. State defaults explicitly (`so_required = No`).
- Mark deviations with **Deviation:** and the reason (scope, simplicity, multi-tenancy, Postgres).
- Checklists use `- [ ]` items at doctype granularity so they can be turned into GitHub issues.
